<%#
  The Repositories section — one entry per git working tree found inside the project's folder,
  never descended: Maker::ProjectFolderListing's walk stops at a `.git` marker and reports the
  directory as a Repo instead of entering it, because a checked-out firmware repo is one thing in a
  project, not three hundred source files filed under "Code". Local: repos
  (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Repo — node_id, name, path).

  ALWAYS OPEN AND NEVER EMPTY-CHECKED HERE: _attachments.html.erb only renders this partial when
  @listing.repos is present, the same rule every other optional section in the panel follows.

  A REPO TILE IS NOT A FILE TILE, deliberately. It carries no thumb_cell_data/file_menu_data (there
  is nothing to poll a thumbnail for and no right-click "Edit in…" for a directory) and no
  tile-meta corner (a repository is not attached or detached the way a file is — its files come and
  go with the working tree). It links straight into the Files browser at that folder, the same
  navigation `files/_grid.html.erb` gives an ordinary folder card.
%>
<section class="attachment-group">
  <details open>
    <summary class="attachment-group-head">
      Repositories <span class="muted">(<%= repos.size %>)</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="attachments-grid">
      <% repos.each do |repo| %>
        <div class="attachment-tile repo-tile">
          <%= link_to files_path(folder: repo.node_id), class: "grid-card" do %>
            <span class="thumb generic-thumb" aria-hidden="true">REPO</span>
            <span class="grid-name"><%= repo.name %></span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
</section>
